```json name=.vscode/settings.json
{
  "github.copilot.enable": {
    "*": false
  }
}
```

```yaml name=.github/workflows/block-copilotignore.yml
name: Block copilotignore files on PR

on:
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review]

jobs:
  deny-copilotignore:
    name: Fail PR if files under copilotignore are present
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Checkout PR
        uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0

      - name: Determine changed files and fail if forbidden files are present
        env:
          BASE_SHA: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail

          echo "Base SHA: $BASE_SHA"
          echo "Listing changed files between base and head..."

          if git rev-parse --verify "$BASE_SHA" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
            git diff --name-only "$BASE_SHA"...HEAD > changed-files.txt || true
          else
            git fetch origin "${{ github.event.pull_request.base.ref }}" --no-tags --depth=1 || true
            git diff --name-only FETCH_HEAD...HEAD > changed-files.txt || true
          fi

          echo "Changed files:"
          cat changed-files.txt

          matches=$(grep -E '(^__copilotignore__/|^copilotignore/)' changed-files.txt || true)

          if [ -n "$matches" ]; then
            echo "::error ::This pull request modifies files under __copilotignore__/ or copilotignore/. Commits adding or changing files inside those folders are blocked by repository policy."
            echo "Matching paths:"
            echo "$matches"
            exit 1
          fi

          echo "No forbidden paths detected."
```

I’ve provided the exact contents for both files so you can paste them into the GitHub editor. Next, in the GitHub page for each “create new file” link paste the corresponding block, choose “Create a new branch for this commit and start a pull request” (recommended), and commit — that will open a PR you can merge once everything looks good.
